rd Panel?Copy the panel's ["get-help" data](https://grafana.com/docs/grafana/latest/troubleshooting/send-panel-to-grafana-support/) here### Grafana Platform?None### User's OS?_No response_### User's Browser?_No response_### Is this a Regression?No### Are Datasources involved?Google Cloud Monitor### Anything else to add?_No response_ | If you create a template variable for a Google Cloud Monitoring project and then create another template variable that references that project variable that variable will change to the "default project" instead of being the project variable. You can see the dropdown value changing from `$project` to the default project name in the GIF below:![Peek 2023-04-13 14-59](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/231857426-7634dd6a-ba0d-4f75-a424-107337b9a485.gif) | <!--Please use this template to create your bug report. By providing as much info as possible you help us understand the issue, reproduce it and resolve it for you quicker. Therefore take a couple of extra minutes to make sure you have provided all info needed.PROTIP: record your screen and attach it as a gif to showcase the issue.- Questions should be posted to: https://community.grafana.com- Use query inspector to troubleshoot issues: https://bit.ly/2XNF6YS- How to record and attach gif: https://bit.ly/2Mi8T6K-->**What happened**:After upgrade to Grafana 9.4.1   (from version 9.3.1), a dashboard based on worldmap plugin and json to api datasource is no more working.  The dashboard use a variable that is based on query from Azure Datasource + a regex  as mentionned in this tuto https://medium.com/@tomjohnburton/visualising-a-distributed-network-c36871da52afSince the upgrade, the variable is no more working  and I get the following message "Templating [ip]Error updating options: Cannot assign to read only property 'resources' of object '#<Object>'"![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/32105900/230117505-d9d8289b-a020-449b-a776-106160734aea.png)![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/32105900/230118514-1326365d-88a3-4f61-a3c4-783da4fe89a0.png)The issue is not reproduced on version 9.3.xThe proxy mode is enable for the datasources : - json to api - Azure MonitorThe configuration of the variable![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/32105900/230120054-8dc734db-337c-4bb1-ba9b-d46c37a436df.png)**What you expected to happen**:Same behaviour thant 9.3 **How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:**Anything else we need to know?**:**Environment**:- Grafana version: 9.4.x - Data source type & version: Azure Monitor (latest)- OS Grafana is installed on: container - User OS & Browser:- Grafana plugins:- Others: | **What happened**:The error: `Error updating options: Cannot add property resources, object is not extensible.` is thrown after upgrading to 9.4.**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:1. In 9.3.x create a template variable, e.g. ```kqlAzureActivity| where SubscriptionId == "$subs"| distinct ResourceGroup| project Value = tostring(ResourceGroup), Text = tostring(ResourceGroup)```2. Upgrade to 9.44. Load the variables editor and note the error![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/222171264-2cea3012-4d87-44f3-b471-4d28e7c21c7c.png)The issue appears to be that the `query` object is not `writeable` during query migration which means creating the `resources` property fails. | **What happened**:Inspecting data for a MQL query that contains an aggregation function causes a crash![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/221231041-af86bf0f-3ede-46ec-838e-c2956378c7f6.png)**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:1. Write a MQL query that uses an aggregation function, e.g. `fetch gce_instance::compute.googleapis.com/instance/cpu/utilization | sum`2. Inspect data3. Crash**Anything else we need to know?**:Similar to #35999 | The link that opens the file picker is set to `tabindex=0` which makes it not accessible via keyboard.![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/194577006-1742e2d3-79b2-41ba-9508-362287247b51.png) | Some of our tooltips are not accessible (you can tab over them to display the help text)- [x] Cloud monitoring query editor (builder)- [x] Template variables editor (Fixed by new layout in Grafana 9.3.0)- [x] ADX client secret (config editor)- [x] ~~ADX query builder~~ (Cannot repro)**Screenshots**<img width="500" alt="Screenshot 2022-10-14 at 21 30 47" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/42030685/195928865-8b19e5a3-3bd0-41ed-a393-cc3d433d610a.png"><img width="500" alt="Screenshot 2022-10-14 at 21 38 24" src="https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/42030685/195929003-9d1e291b-35ef-4e2c-b582-0c9678739dce.png"> | After the Grafana 9.0.0 and these changes https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/49029. It is not possible to find/chose custom Metric Namespaces.We have a namespaces named "Yggdrasil ServiceBus Metrics", which we could find and chose before, but now it's not possible - not even when typing it in manually.![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/43808309/188612157-67fb1e49-d2cf-4dbe-ae9c-aa0409d11622.png)Not able to find or query it:![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/43808309/188610692-c618925e-5eca-4c28-b149-23c30afbaaa4.png)With Grafana < 9.0.0 it worked perfectly fine and we could chose it from the picker. | add an integration tests like it is done for prometheus in https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/pkg/tests/api/prometheus/prometheus_test.goto make sure headers are correctly sent.for more details see https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/54314 | This will make the experimental UI work the default/baseline UI experience for AzureMonitor (effectively finish https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/44432)We should also remove the fixed widths on the metrics selects to enable the metrics + aggregation + time grain to be on the first row.![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/178069070-1cfe1cc6-252d-4087-9306-8bfac7bbfc3e.png) | Related to #44432Specifically two areas:- What should go in the "header" area?- Usage regarding `EditorRows`. | Related to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/44432[Feature toggle docs](https://github.com/grafana/deployment_tools/blob/master/ksonnet/environments/hosted-grafana/waves/feature-toggles/README.md) | > we should provide a template variable query function for listing log groups so that the user doesn't have to add them manually using a custom variable.- https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/49737#pullrequestreview-989306355- [ ] Add template variable query function- [ ] Update docs | Related to https://github.com/grafana/grafana/issues/44432 | Related to #44432Migrate Logs to use the [grafana/grafana-experimental](github.com/grafana/grafana-experimental) UI.This includes:- the Resource selector- the Format selector | Related to #44432Migrate Metrics to use the [grafana/grafana-experimental](github.com/grafana/grafana-experimental) UI.This includes grouping the following fields together:1. Resources  - Group  - Type  - Name2. Metrics  - namespace  - metric3. Aggregation  - Time grain4. Dimension![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/1048831/166703986-33243560-fcda-4e8f-b920-87e983d24304.png)6. Top7. Legend Format | <!--Please use this template to create your bug report. By providing as much info as possible you help us understand the issue, reproduce it and resolve it for you quicker. Therefore take a couple of extra minutes to make sure you have provided all info needed.PROTIP: record your screen and attach it as a gif to showcase the issue.- Questions should be posted to: https://community.grafana.com- Use query inspector to troubleshoot issues: https://bit.ly/2XNF6YS- How to record and attach gif: https://bit.ly/2Mi8T6K-->**What happened**:The link in the tooltip for "Regex" in the Variable Editor isn't clickable. ![regex-tooltip](https://user-images.githubuserc