you expected to happen**:The data source to be validated again, with the same credentials.**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:**Anything else we need to know?**:**Environment**:- Grafana version: 9.0.0-pre- Data source type & version:- OS Grafana is installed on:- User OS & Browser:- Grafana plugins:- Others: | The [annotation editor](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/public/app/plugins/datasource/cloud-monitoring/components/AnnotationQueryEditor.tsx) in the CloudMonitoring plugin is written in react. However, when it was initially built there was only API support for registering annotation editors written in angular.This is similar to #47457 This PR :Uses the new API (registering react annotation editors in the datasource file) for registering the annotation editor in the CloudMonitoring datasourceRemoves what's left of angularProgress following mob sessions 14/04/22Removed .setAnnotationQueryCtrl from module.tsAdded annotation object in datasource.ts with a QueryEditor that's using the existing AnnotationQueryEditorNext Steps:Fix typing issues- Try changing the AnnotationQueryEditor state type to CloudMonitoringQuery? | <!--Please use this template to create your bug report. By providing as much info as possible you help us understand the issue, reproduce it and resolve it for you quicker. Therefore take a couple of extra minutes to make sure you have provided all info needed.PROTIP: record your screen and attach it as a gif to showcase the issue.- Questions should be posted to: https://community.grafana.com- Use query inspector to troubleshoot issues: https://bit.ly/2XNF6YS- How to record and attach gif: https://bit.ly/2Mi8T6K-->**What happened**:When a logs query is edited it doesn't run unless the refresh button is hit for the panel, even if it's a valid query.**What you expected to happen**:When the Log Groups are changed or the text query is blurred it should call `onRunQuery`. Alternatively, a run query button could be added to the editor that calls `onRunQuery`.**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:Open a panel for a Cloudwatch log query and set values for Log Groups and the text query (the help button can autofill one)**Anything else we need to know?**:**Environment**:- Grafana version:- Data source type & version:- OS Grafana is installed on:- User OS & Browser:- Grafana plugins:- Others: | **Steps to reproduce**:When tab-ing our way through the datasource creation page, we will lose focus between a textbox and another (where the switch is). Non blocking as we can still toggle the switch but very tedious in `Auth` section as it's 6 switch and we don't see where we are when using tabs**Actual Result**:switch not focussed**Expected Result**we should see the switch focus state (highlighted) . This could be achieved using the `InlineSwitch` component instead of `Switch` or by modifying `Switch` to be accessible.Gio Ricci started a PR for that during the Hackathon week: #46252 **Relevant WCAG Criteria:** [2.4.7 Focus visible - Level AA](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG21/quickref/?versions=2.0&showtechniques=335%2C332#focus-visible)**Environment**:- Grafana version: 8.4.3 | The goal is to remove the use of `simplejson` and use unmarshalling.The [consensus](https://github.com/grafana/grafana/blob/main/contribute/style-guides/backend.md#json) is that new Go code shouldn't use `simplejson`. Therefore we also want to iteratively factor it out where it already exists in the codebase. Instead of relying on yet another library for this we should instead use the standard library's `encoding/json` capabilities and define native Go structs to hold the JSON. An example of this type of work can be found in #34952.The approach should look something like: - Start in `pkg/tsdb/cloudwatch/cloudwatch.go` (or another entry point, it doesn't really matter)- Find where `simplejson` is used, e.g. in `QueryData`.- Create a struct to define the shape of the JSON that we're expecting. It can be helpful to look at where `simplejson` helper methods are used to get a sense of what properties are expected, e.g. `model.Get("metricName").String()` shows that `metricName` should be defined in the struct.- Let the test failures guide the rest of the work and/or verify things are working by clicking through the UI. Done is when `simplejson` isn't present in any CloudWatch files and tests still pass.Non exhaustive list of places to shore up with tests:- [x] Add tests to annotations query- [x] Add tests to executeStartQuery- [ ] executeLogAlertQuery is virtually untested. Add first minimal test #46243- [ ] Add tests on the values set in "model" in executeLogAlertQuery | Similarly to the CloudWatch metrics query editor, we should refactor the Azure Monitor query editor so that it's using the new query editor UI components from the [grafana-experimental](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-experimental) repo. Would be good if we could involve UX in this work. ---Here's the roadmap of issues since we've changed this to an epic- [x] #48709- [x] #48711- [x] #48713- [x] #50170 - [x] #50171- [ ] #52003 | Similarly to the CloudWatch metrics query editor, we should refactor the CloudMonitoring query editor so that it's using the new query editor UI components from the [grafana-experimental](https://github.com/grafana/grafana-experimental) repo. Would be good if we could involve UX in this work.  | **What happened**:Grafana crashes while switching back to query type variable**How to reproduce it (as minimally and precisely as possible)**:Steps:1. Click on Dashboard settings -> variables2. Add new variable. It should be Query type3. Choose Azure Monitor data source4. Change to Custom type5. Change back to Query type`grafanaTemplateVariableFns.ts:226 Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Cannot read properties of undefined (reading ‘defaultSubscriptionId’)`![out](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/4163034/147356989-9f686fac-0b27-49a1-a2fc-cb1e0b4cc8e2.gif)**Environment**:Grafana version: 8.4-pre | <!--Please use this template to create your bug report. By providing as much info as possible you help us understand the issue, reproduce it and resolve it for you quicker. Therefor take a couple of extra minutes to make sure you have provided all info needed.PROTIP: record your
